 @atindex @code{interrupt_handler}, V850
 @item interrupt
 @itemx interrupt_handler
+@itemx interrupt ("@var{level}")
+@itemx interrupt_handler ("@var{level}")
 This attribute applies to functions.
 
 Use these attributes to indicate
@@ -8732,6 +8734,19 @@ that the specified function is an interrupt handler.  The compiler generates
 function entry and exit sequences suitable for use in an interrupt handler
 when either attribute is present.
 
+For @option{-mv850e3v5} and later, the optional argument @var{level}
+selects the exception level of the handler.  With no argument or
+@code{"EI"}, the handler returns with @code{eiret}; with @code{"FE"}, it
+returns with @code{feret}.  The argument is not accepted for earlier
+targets, which return with @code{reti}.
+
+An EI level handler saves and restores EIPC and EIPSW, so that it can
+enable interrupts with @code{ei} and be nested; interrupts are disabled
+again before EIPC and EIPSW are restored.  An FE level handler does not
+save FEPC and FEPSW@.  A handler saves FPSR and FPEPC when it uses the
+FPU or calls a function, and with @option{-mfxu} it saves FXSR when it
+calls a function.
+
 @atindex @code{sda}, V850
 @item sda
 This attribute applies to variables.
